    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">SOIL TEMPERATURE</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2021-08-31 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=reference 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=American Meteorological Society Glossary of Meteorology Online
&quot;http://amsglossary.allenpress.com/glossary&quot;
New Value=The Nature and Properties of Soils, Prentice Hall, 1996.</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2021-08-31 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=The temperature measured at a given soil depth, typically at 2, 4, 8, and
sometimes 20 and 40 in. 
Many biological processes, including seed germination, plant emergence,
microbial activity, and soil respiration are a function of soil temperature.
New Value=The degree of hotness or coldness of the soil as measured on some definite temperature scale.</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="The Nature and Properties of Soils, Prentice Hall, 1996." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The degree of hotness or coldness of the soil as measured on some definite temperature scale.</skos:definition>
