    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">GEOMAGNETIC STORM CATEGORY</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-02-18 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=GEOMAGNETIC STORM CATEGORY [4b7decec-e378-4824-aecf-9fe509392efd,82401] - GEOMAGNETIC FORECASTS [02290e22-24ae-40f6-96f1-0c6c76a145af,63913]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-03-11 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: A category or scale that describe the environmental disturbances for three event types: geomagnetic storms, solar radiation storms, and radio blackouts. The scales have numbered levels, analogous to hurricanes, tornadoes, and earthquakes that convey severity. They list possible effects at each level. They also show how often such events happen, and give a measure of the intensity of the physical causes.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="NOAA" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A category or scale that describe the environmental disturbances for three event types: geomagnetic storms, solar radiation storms, and radio blackouts. The scales have numbered levels, analogous to hurricanes, tornadoes, and earthquakes that convey severity. They list possible effects at each level. They also show how often such events happen, and give a measure of the intensity of the physical causes.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2013-03-11 14:28:47.0</dcterms:modified>
