    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">SATURATION VAPOR PRESSURE</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2017-04-20 User Id=sritz Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=SATURATION VAPOR PRESSURE [1a2332d9-fd69-4002-89a5-203d748a4e21,278829] - WATER VAPOR INDICATORS [005d192a-95b9-4fc2-afed-f87da3c3dc33,278815]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2017-04-21 User Id=sritz Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: The vapor pressure of a system, at a given temperature, for which the vapor of a substance is in equilibrium with a plane surface of that substance&apos;s pure liquid or solid phase; that is, the vapor pressure of a system that has attained saturation but not supersaturation.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Glossary of Meteorology, American Meteorological Society" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The vapor pressure of a system, at a given temperature, for which the vapor of a substance is in equilibrium with a plane surface of that substance&apos;s pure liquid or solid phase; that is, the vapor pressure of a system that has attained saturation but not supersaturation.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2017-04-21 13:20:42.0</dcterms:modified>
