  <skos:Concept rdf:about="05410006-351a-4877-96e8-f0a821161ecf">
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="b73cee46-8e2c-4df9-b1ed-7f0aa98a04ac"/>
    <dcterms:created>2012-06-26</dcterms:created>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">GEOTHERMAL ENERGY PRODUCTION/USE</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-06-29 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Refers to the production and use of geothermal energy for human consumption. Geothermal energy is energy extracted from heat stored in the earth. This geothermal energy originates from the original formation of the planet, from radioactive decay of minerals, and from solar energy absorbed at the surface.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-06-26 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=GEOTHERMAL ENERGY PRODUCTION/USE [05410006-351a-4877-96e8-f0a821161ecf,40127] - ENERGY PRODUCTION/USE [b73cee46-8e2c-4df9-b1ed-7f0aa98a04ac,40101]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="U.S. Department of Energy" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Refers to the production and use of geothermal energy for human consumption. Geothermal energy is energy extracted from heat stored in the earth. This geothermal energy originates from the original formation of the planet, from radioactive decay of minerals, and from solar energy absorbed at the surface.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2012-06-29 13:45:46.0</dcterms:modified>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="069ff99d-1455-4285-83d9-4f57fb0cb635">
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="a200e677-384a-42d6-8519-1c7735f0adb9"/>
    <dcterms:created>2016-06-28</dcterms:created>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">TORNADO PATH WIDTH</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2016-06-28 User Id=saritz Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=TORNADO PATH WIDTH [069ff99d-1455-4285-83d9-4f57fb0cb635,217721] - TORNADOES [a200e677-384a-42d6-8519-1c7735f0adb9,84177]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2016-06-28 User Id=saritz Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Path length (in miles and tenths of miles) and maximum path width (in yards) will be indicated for all tornadoes, including each member of families of tornadoes, or for all segments of multi-segmented tornadoes. The length in the header-strip is the length of that particular segment in that particular county/parish. The Storm Prediction Center, NCDC or a Storm Data user can determine the entire length of a multi-segmented tornado by adding the lengths from each segment as well as using the latitude and longitude of that segment. Note that latitude and longitude are not available in the Storm Data publication, but are available on the internet in National Climatic Data 
Center and the Storm Prediction Center databases.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="NOAA National Weather Service Instructions 10-1605 Section 7.40.0" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Path length (in miles and tenths of miles) and maximum path width (in yards) will be indicated for all tornadoes, including each member of families of tornadoes, or for all segments of multi-segmented tornadoes. The length in the header-strip is the length of that particular segment in that particular county/parish. The Storm Prediction Center, NCDC or a Storm Data user can determine the entire length of a multi-segmented tornado by adding the lengths from each segment as well as using the latitude and longitude of that segment. Note that latitude and longitude are not available in the Storm Data publication, but are available on the internet in National Climatic Data Center and the Storm Prediction Center databases.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2016-06-28 14:01:25.0</dcterms:modified>
