    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-08-20 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: A measure of a rock&apos;s ability to hold a fluid. Mathematically, porosity is the open space in a rock divided by the total rock volume (solid +  space or holes). Porosity is normally expressed as a percentage of the total rock which is taken up by pore space.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
