    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A measure of a rock&apos;s ability to hold a fluid. Mathematically, porosity is the open space in a rock divided by the total rock volume (solid +  space or holes). Porosity is normally expressed as a percentage of the total rock which is taken up by pore space.</skos:definition>
