  <skos:Concept rdf:about="02e08d51-9b6b-4412-9119-0a70207f8e87">
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="1a6ed5fe-608e-46a0-ab9e-1306de875ebe"/>
    <dcterms:created>2024-03-01</dcterms:created>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">AMPLICON SEQUENCE VARIANT (ASV)</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-03-01 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: ASVs are clusters of sequences with 100% identity of both sequence content and length, allowing some modeled error. ASVs are made using denoising methods that generate an error model based on the quality of the sequencing run and use this model to distinguish between the predicted “true” biological variation and that likely generated by sequencing error. The remaining “true” sequences vary from as little as one single nucleotide and are then defined as separate ASVs.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-03-01 User Id=tstevens Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=AMPLICON SEQUENCE VARIANT _ASV_ [02e08d51-9b6b-4412-9119-0a70207f8e87,1603394] - METAGENOME [1a6ed5fe-608e-46a0-ab9e-1306de875ebe,1603392]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-03-01 User Id=tstevens Entity=PrefLabel Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
System Note=update PrefLabel
Old Value=AMPLICON SEQUENCE VARIANT _ASV_
New Value=AMPLICON SEQUENCE VARIANT (ASV)</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0264443" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">ASVs are clusters of sequences with 100% identity of both sequence content and length, allowing some modeled error. ASVs are made using denoising methods that generate an error model based on the quality of the sequencing run and use this model to distinguish between the predicted “true” biological variation and that likely generated by sequencing error. The remaining “true” sequences vary from as little as one single nucleotide and are then defined as separate ASVs.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2024-03-01 13:04:29.0</dcterms:modified>
