    <skos:broader rdf:resource="3f4cfc81-7745-43d9-b313-f68cdf72359b"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">GAS EXPLOSIONS/LEAKS</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-06-29 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=reference 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=Global Explosion Consultants  http://www.gexcon.com &quot;Gas leak&quot; definition
adapted from the American Gas &amp; Chemical Co. Ltd. http://www.amgas.com
New Value=Global Explosion Consultants  http://www.gexcon.com &quot;Gas leak&quot; definition adapted from the American Gas &amp; Chemical Co. Ltd. http://www.amgas.com</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-06-29 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=A gas explosion is defined as a process where combustion of a premixed
gas-air cloud causes a rapid increase of pressure. Gas explosions may
occur inside process equipment or pipes, in buildings or off-shore
modules, in open process areas or in unconfined areas. A gas is leak
is the diffusion of a gas through a hole or porosity in an enclosure
capable of passing a fluid from the higher pressure side to the
lower pressure side.
New Value=A gas explosion is defined as a process where combustion of a premixed gas-air, cloud causes a rapid increase of pressure.</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-06-29 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=A gas explosion is defined as a process where combustion of a premixed gas-air, cloud causes a rapid increase of pressure.
New Value=A gas explosion is defined as a process where combustion of a premixed gas-air cloud causes a rapid increase of pressure.</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Global Explosion Consultants  http://www.gexcon.com &apos;Gas leak&apos; definition adapted from the American Gas &amp; Chemical Co. Ltd. http://www.amgas.com" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A gas explosion is defined as a process where combustion of a premixed gas-air cloud causes a rapid increase of pressure.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2012-06-29 14:42:39.0</dcterms:modified>
