    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">ISOTOPE MEASUREMENTS</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-03-11 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: The measure of Isotopes, atoms that contain different # of proton /neutrons. The number of protons (the atomic number) is the same for each isotope, e.g. carbon-12, carbon-13 and carbon-14 each have 6 protons, but the number of neutrons in each isotope differs.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-02-18 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=ISOTOPE MEASUREMENTS [849edfe2-9ed7-4211-8f57-9c8ccff0a4ea,82363] - GEOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES [048df94e-841d-4f4d-a5c5-6683d1d07aa6,82357]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="American Chemical Society" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The measure of Isotopes, atoms that contain different # of proton /neutrons. The number of protons (the atomic number) is the same for each isotope, e.g. carbon-12, carbon-13 and carbon-14 each have 6 protons, but the number of neutrons in each isotope differs.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2013-03-11 13:34:25.0</dcterms:modified>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
