  <skos:Concept rdf:about="38cefcb2-f5d6-4917-a87b-7cfba482e30d">
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="06180441-d4bb-4fed-b36a-9b3cb2cac0fe"/>
    <dcterms:created>2016-06-28</dcterms:created>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">MINIMUM CENTRAL PRESSURE</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2016-07-31 User Id=saritz Entity=NarrowerRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add narrower relation
New Value=MINIMUM CENTRAL PRESSURE [38cefcb2-f5d6-4917-a87b-7cfba482e30d,217795] - HURRICANES  (N. ATLANTIC/E. PACIFIC) [3b1544bc-1711-4553-a643-5d8fba38a1f1,247561]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2016-07-31 User Id=saritz Entity=NarrowerRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add narrower relation
New Value=MINIMUM CENTRAL PRESSURE [38cefcb2-f5d6-4917-a87b-7cfba482e30d,217795] - SEVERE TROPICAL CYCLONES (SW PACIFIC/SE INDIAN) [5b70e02b-0ed2-42a0-9fe9-7a552d6819d1,247565]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2016-06-28 User Id=saritz Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: The atmospheric pressure at the center of a high or low.  It is the highest pressure in a high and the lowest pressure in a low, referring to the sea level pressure of the system.   In a hurricane, a lower central pressure create a stronger gradient from outside to inside the system.  The stronger this pressure gradient is, the greater the maximum wind speeds around the eye wall.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2016-06-28 User Id=saritz Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
