    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Southeast Coastal Ocean Observing Regional Association (SECOORA) Hurricane Glossary." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:narrower rdf:resource="cfb85bf2-9920-4e3f-bce3-3d8f68ab1436"/>
    <skos:narrower rdf:resource="50abff20-11a8-4aea-8425-c9a05b1d8d09"/>
    <skos:narrower rdf:resource="5b70e02b-0ed2-42a0-9fe9-7a552d6819d1"/>
    <skos:narrower rdf:resource="3b1544bc-1711-4553-a643-5d8fba38a1f1"/>
    <skos:narrower rdf:resource="ef467c3c-0aed-4aa8-bfa5-67721e83e557"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The atmospheric pressure at the center of a high or low.  It is the highest pressure in a high and the lowest pressure in a low, referring to the sea level pressure of the system.   In a hurricane, a lower central pressure create a stronger gradient from outside to inside the system.  The stronger this pressure gradient is, the greater the maximum wind speeds around the eye wall.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2016-07-31 20:06:03.0</dcterms:modified>
