    <skos:narrower rdf:resource="c310aa65-810b-4e36-9689-d37b1154fa1b"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Birds, of the class Aves, are warm-blooded craniates with a body coveringof feathers; typically with forelimbs modified as wings for active flight.They are free living (most can fly) in all terrestrial and surface waterhabitats; some are capable of swimming underwater.</skos:definition>
