    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">SEDIMENT CHEMISTRY</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-02-18 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=SEDIMENT CHEMISTRY [09b4427b-9e8b-413a-83cd-f087b284cf61,82483] - SEDIMENTATION [984e15c6-7eac-45b8-b098-ad82eab6be6e,82481]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Refers to the chemical makeup and characteristics of sediments. In chemistry, sedimentation has been used to measure the size of large molecules (macromolecule), where the force of gravity is augmented with centrifugal force in an ultracentrifuge.</skos:definition>
