Old Value=METHANE [0948a59e-cc72-4e5d-b97d-4ea0335b0906,40141] - NITROUS OXIDE [bc90bc40-2a21-4a6f-9fb9-bf3ae5845157,40143]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-07-23 User Id=mpmorahan Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Methane (CH4) is a greenhouse gas and is seen in polar ice cores. From the ice core record, it is known that methane rose rapidly whenever climate changed from glacial to interglacial conditions (during &quot;deglaciation&quot;). Warming of water bathing the seafloor could have led to large-scale release of methane from the melting of methane ice.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Glossary of climate change  http://calspace.ucsd.edu  See also:  http://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/paleo/icecore/antarctica/vostok/vostok_methane.html" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Methane (CH4) is a greenhouse gas and is seen in polar ice cores. From the ice core record, it is known that methane rose rapidly whenever climate changed from glacial to interglacial conditions (during &apos;deglaciation&apos;). Warming of water bathing the seafloor could have led to large-scale release of methane from the melting of methane ice.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2012-07-23 15:55:11.0</dcterms:modified>
