    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Raynaud, D., Jouzel, J., Barnola, J. M., Chappellaz, J., Delmas, R. J. &amp;  Lorius, C. (1993) Science 259, 926-933.  20. Battle, M., Bender, M., Sowers, T., Tans, P. P., Butler, J. H., Elkins,  J. W., Ellis, J. T., Conway, T., Zhang, N., Lang, P. &amp; Clarke, A. D. (1996)  Nature (London) 383, 231-23.  Referenced in Alley, Richard B. Ice-core evidence of abrupt climate changes,  Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America  (http://www.pnas.org/cgi/content/full/97/4/1331?ijkey=JifxlJJnHUR2Q)" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Trapped gases in ice-core bubbles are highly reliable records of atmospheric composition in reconstructing past climates.</skos:definition>
