text: Formed when a glacier cuts a U-shaped valley by abrasion of the surrounding bedrock. Many such valleys were formed during the recent ice age. Glacial melting is accompanied by rebound of Earth&apos;s crust as the ice load and eroded sediment is removed (also called isostasy or glacial rebound).
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-08-06 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=FJORDS [7299f45f-eafb-4ed9-ae12-5e01c97c1530,105523] - COASTAL LANDFORMS [0cff6e4b-e42a-4565-89ff-350adf41ed69,105283]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="PhysicalGeography.net" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Formed when a glacier cuts a U-shaped valley by abrasion of the surrounding bedrock. Many such valleys were formed during the recent ice age. Glacial melting is accompanied by rebound of Earth&apos;s crust as the ice load and eroded sediment is removed (also called isostasy or glacial rebound).</skos:definition>
