System Note=update Definition
Old Value=Unconsolidated particles created by the weathering and erosion of rock, by
chemical precipitation from solution in water, or from the secretions of
organisms, and transported by water, wind, or glaciers.
New Value=Unconsolidated particles created by the weathering and erosion of rock, by chemical precipitation from solution in water, or from the secretions of organisms, and transported by water, wind, or glaciers.</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Lutgens, Frederick K., Edward J. Tarbuck.  Essentials of Geology, 5th Edition. Prentice-Hall, Inc.:  Englewood Cliffs, NJ, 1995." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Unconsolidated particles created by the weathering and erosion of rock, by chemical precipitation from solution in water, or from the secretions of organisms, and transported by water, wind, or glaciers.</skos:definition>
