    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Lutgens, Frederick K., Edward J. Tarbuck.  Essentials of Geology, 5th Edition. Prentice-Hall, Inc.:  Englewood Cliffs, NJ, 1995." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Unconsolidated particles created by the weathering and erosion of rock,by chemical precipitation from solution in water, or from the secretionsof organisms, and transported by water, wind, or glaciers.</skos:definition>
