    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-08-20 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=An environment in the upper coastal intertidal zone between land and salty or brackish water, dominated by dense stands of halophytic  (salt-tolerant) plants such as herbs, grasses, or low shrubs.
New Value=Sea arches form by wave erosion of coastal headlands. Sea arches are very temporary landforms, in both geologic and human terms.</skos:changeNote>
