New Value=id: null
text: Microfossils are fossils too small to be seen without the aid of a microscope, e.g., a foraminifer or ostracode. It may be the remains of microscopic organisms or a part of a larger orgnaism.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Jackson, J.A., ed. 1997. Glossary of Geology. American Geological Institute" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Microfossils are fossils too small to be seen without the aid of a microscope, e.g., a foraminifer or ostracode. It may be the remains of microscopic organisms or a part of a larger orgnaism.</skos:definition>
