    <skos:changeNote>Date=2017-03-10 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=Active layer, also called frost zone or mollisol is that part of the soil
included with the suprapermafrost layer (i.e., existing above permafrost) that
usually freezes in winter and thaws in summer.
New Value=Active layer, also called frost zone or mollisol is that part of the soil included with the suprapermafrost layer (i.e., existing above permafrost) that usually freezes in winter and thaws in summer.</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="American Meteorological Society Glossary of Meteorology. &apos;http://amsglossary.allenpress.com/glossary&apos;" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Active layer, also called frost zone or mollisol is that part of the soil included with the suprapermafrost layer (i.e., existing above permafrost) that usually freezes in winter and thaws in summer.</skos:definition>
