    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">FRESH WATER RIVER DISCHARGE</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-07-05 User Id=mpmorahan Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: discharge is the volume rate of water flow, including any suspended solids (i.e. sediment), dissolved chemical species (i.e. CaCO3(aq)) and/or biologic material (i.e. diatoms), which is transported through a given cross-sectional area.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-06-26 User Id=gee-cee Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=FRESH WATER RIVER DISCHARGE [12dc1f4f-2116-4b74-a1bd-bc61e8e57a5b,39821] - ATMOSPHERIC/OCEAN INDICATORS [5273c8c2-d30b-4666-b2d5-0388ce2741d0,39645]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Buchanan, T.J. and Somers, W.P., 1969, Discharge Measurements at Gaging Stations: U.S. Geological Survey Techniques of Water-Resources Investigations, Book 3, Chapter A8, 1p. Wikipedia: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Discharge_%28hydrology%29#cite_note-0" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">discharge is the volume rate of water flow, including any suspended solids (i.e. sediment), dissolved chemical species (i.e. CaCO3(aq)) and/or biologic material (i.e. diatoms), which is transported through a given cross-sectional area.</skos:definition>
