    <skos:changeNote>Date=2014-04-14 User Id=128.183.164.42 Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
User Note=added definition
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=Drizzle, falling as a liquid, but freezing on impact with the colder ground or other exposed surfaces. It is reported as &quot;FZDZ&quot; in an observation and on the METAR.
New Value=Drizzle that falls in liquid form but freezes upon impact to form a coating of glaze.</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Glossary of Meteorology, American Meteorological Society, 2013,  http://glossary.ametsoc.org/wiki/Freezing_drizzle" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Drizzle that falls in liquid form but freezes upon impact to form a coating of glaze.</skos:definition>
