    <skos:related rdf:resource="84510f18-a4e6-434c-a54c-44cc995e1af2"/>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="0ff2a38d-00f6-459d-ac9a-9a983bda602e">
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="76b8c21c-c221-4724-86ef-c07222cb152b"/>
    <dcterms:created>2012-06-26</dcterms:created>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">ICE GROWTH/MELT</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-06-26 User Id=gee-cee Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=ICE GROWTH/MELT [0ff2a38d-00f6-459d-ac9a-9a983bda602e,39929] - CRYOSPHERIC INDICATORS [76b8c21c-c221-4724-86ef-c07222cb152b,39899]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-07-10 User Id=mpmorahan Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Melt of the ice can occur at various stages: puddle, thaw holes, dried ice, rotten ice, flodded ice, and frozen puddle. Developing sea ice (or growth) takes on the following stages: New Ice, Youg Ice, First-Year Ice, Old Ice. Lake Ice development goes through the following stages: New Lake Ice, Thin Lake Ice, Medium Lake Ice, Thick Lake Ice, and Very Thick Lake Ice.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Canadian Ice Service - Environment Canada http://www.cis.ec.gc.ca/manice/chp1_eng.htm" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Melt of the ice can occur at various stages: puddle, thaw holes, dried ice, rotten ice, flodded ice, and frozen puddle. Developing sea ice (or growth) takes on the following stages: New Ice, Youg Ice, First-Year Ice, Old Ice. Lake Ice development goes through the following stages: New Lake Ice, Thin Lake Ice, Medium Lake Ice, Thick Lake Ice, and Very Thick Lake Ice.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2012-07-10 13:50:15.0</dcterms:modified>
