    <skos:changeNote>Date=2017-03-15 User Id=mgenazzi Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
User Note=Definition updated
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=A set of deposited sedimentary beds that reflects the depositional environment.
New Value=A set of deposited sedimentary beds that reflects the depositional environment of those beds and the geologic history of a region. A stratigraphic sequence is a chronologic succession of sedimentary rocks from older below to younger above without interruption.</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Adapted from: Press, F. and Siever, R. 1986. Earth. W.H. Freeman and Company. Fourth Edition. p. 645." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A set of deposited sedimentary beds that reflects the depositional environment of those beds and the geologic history of a region. A stratigraphic sequence is a chronologic succession of sedimentary rocks from older below to younger above without interruption.</skos:definition>
