    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-08-26 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: End moraines, or terminal moraines, are ridges of unconsolidated debris deposited at the snout or end of the glacier. They usually reflect the shape of the glacier&apos;s terminus.  Glaciers act much like a conveyor belt, carrying debris from the top of the glacier to the bottom where it deposits it in end moraines.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-08-06 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=TERMINAL MORAINE [16bd425e-9a14-41ac-900e-5b5c4f713dda,105653] - MORAINES [2575cfaf-1a09-48b6-acb9-fda23b6f4719,105627]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="PhysicalGeography.net" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">End moraines, or terminal moraines, are ridges of unconsolidated debris deposited at the snout or end of the glacier. They usually reflect the shape of the glacier&apos;s terminus.  Glaciers act much like a conveyor belt, carrying debris from the top of the glacier to the bottom where it deposits it in end moraines.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2024-11-06 12:10:41.0</dcterms:modified>
