User Note=Move Concepts
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=BAROMETRIC ALTITUDE [5d703cfe-2f7c-4736-acbc-ec4e4f4f8eef,20167] - ATMOSPHERE [c47f6052-634e-40ef-a5ac-13f69f6f4c2a,19875]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Glossary of Meteorology, American Meteorological Society, 1998." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Also called Pressure Altitude. Barometric Altitude is the altitude
which corresponds to a given value of atmospheric pressure according to
the ICAO standard atmosphere. It is the indicated altitude of a pressure
altimeter at an altimeter setting of 29.92 inches of mercury (1013.2
mb); therefore it is the indicated altitude above the 1013.2 mb
constant-pressure surface. RT</skos:definition>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
  </skos:Concept>
