    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Glossary of Meteorology, American Meteorological Society, 1998." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The height of the atmospheric layer from the Earth&apos;s surface up to analtitude of about 1 kilometer in which wind speed and direction areaffected by frictional interaction with objects on the Earth&apos;ssurface.</skos:definition>
