    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Glossary of Weather and Climate, American Meteorological Society, 1996." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A type of frozen precipitation in the form of balls or irregular lumps ofice, usually consisting of concentric layers of ice. Hail is alwaysproduced by convective clouds, nearly always cumulonimbus.</skos:definition>
