    <skos:narrower rdf:resource="3375096a-7782-42e8-97d2-0febf63893e0"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Low-level clouds that form in the troposphere, the lowest layer of Earth&apos;s atmosphere, below 6,500 feet and normally consist of liquid water droplets or even supercooled droplets, except during cold winter storms when ice crystals (and snow) comprise much of the clouds.</skos:definition>
