    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">TRANSCRIPTOMIC ANALYSIS</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-02-28 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: The key aims of transcriptomics are: to catalog all species of transcript, including mRNAs, non-coding RNAs and small RNAs; to determine the transcriptional structure of genes, in terms of their start sites, 5′ and 3′ ends, splicing patterns, and other post-transcriptional modifications; and to quantify the changing expression levels of each transcript during development and under different conditions.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-02-28 User Id=tstevens Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=TRANSCRIPTOMIC ANALYSIS [19291970-5f7d-47b0-9101-11b03a15d9ee,1603371] - OMICS METHODOLOGY [d2f152e1-7398-44ad-b0a4-77ee6ef5bd6c,1603367]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC2949280/" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The key aims of transcriptomics are: to catalog all species of transcript, including mRNAs, non-coding RNAs and small RNAs; to determine the transcriptional structure of genes, in terms of their start sites, 5′ and 3′ ends, splicing patterns, and other post-transcriptional modifications; and to quantify the changing expression levels of each transcript during development and under different conditions.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2024-02-28 12:33:08.0</dcterms:modified>
