    <dcterms:created>2013-09-04</dcterms:created>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">COMMON SENSE CLIMATE INDEX</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-09-04 User Id=epneff Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=COMMON SENSE CLIMATE INDEX [1d527151-57b2-49ed-9937-c1756a704ce9,105817] - ATMOSPHERIC TEMPERATURE INDICES [25d73bcf-c8d4-4c0e-ac98-8f3e98677e73,105815]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-10-11 User Id=saritz Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Added new definition.
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Our climate index is a simple measure of the degree, if any, to which practical climate change is occurring.  It also illustrates natural climate variability, thus revealing how difficult it is to reliably perceive a change of quantities that are naturally ‘‘noisy’’ or chaotic. Our aim is to help people judge whether or not climate fluctuations are a significant indication of change and to provide improved understanding of climate variability.

More Information: http://data.giss.nasa.gov/csci/
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="James Hansen, Makiko Sato, Jay Glascoe, and Reto Ruedy, A common-sense climate index: Is climate changing noticeably?, Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA, Vol. 95, pp. 4113– 4120, April 1998." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Our climate index is a simple measure of the degree, if any, to which practical climate change is occurring.  It also illustrates natural climate variability, thus revealing how difficult it is to reliably perceive a change of quantities that are naturally ‘‘noisy’’ or chaotic. Our aim is to help people judge whether or not climate fluctuations are a significant indication of change and to provide improved understanding of climate variability.More Information: http://data.giss.nasa.gov/csci/</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2013-10-11 17:29:03.0</dcterms:modified>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
  </skos:Concept>
