System Note=add broader relation
New Value=RIFTING [1b370af4-1887-4e7a-82a6-9acb9ce5dd5f,105415] - TECTONIC PROCESSES [99b4792a-9ea3-4756-a4dc-b1b30c946b54,86001]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-08-16 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: The process in which continental crust is extended and thinned, forming extensional sedimentary basins and/or mafic dyke-swarms. Rifts commence as intracratonic, down-thrown blocks dominated by normal or oblique-extensional (transtensional) faults.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="World of Earth Science" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The process in which continental crust is extended and thinned, forming extensional sedimentary basins and/or mafic dyke-swarms. Rifts commence as intracratonic, down-thrown blocks dominated by normal or oblique-extensional (transtensional) faults.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2013-08-16 12:10:02.0</dcterms:modified>
