    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">SOIL EROSION</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-09-30 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=reference 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=From the Glossary of Soil Terms/Soil Science Society of America (SSSA):
&quot;http://www.soils.org/sssagloss/&quot;
New Value=From the Glossary of Soil Terms/Soil Science Society of America (SSSA):
&quot;http://www.soils.org/sssagloss/&quot;</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-09-30 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=(i) The wearing away of the land surface by rain or irrigation water, wind,
ice, or other natural or anthropogenic agents that abrade, detach and remove
geologic parent material or soil from one point on the earth&apos;s surface and
deposit it elsewhere, including such processes as gravitational creep and
so-called tillage erosion; (ii) The detachment and movement of soil or rock by
water, wind, ice, or gravity.
New Value=(i) The wearing away of the land surface by rain or irrigation water, wind,
ice, or other natural or anthropogenic agents that abrade, detach and remove
geologic parent material or soil from one point on the earth&apos;s surface and
deposit it elsewhere, including such processes as gravitational creep and
so-called tillage erosion; (ii) The detachment and movement of soil or rock by
water, wind, ice, or gravity.</skos:changeNote>
