relationship value: null
generated by: null</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="From the Glossary of Soil Terms/Soil Science Society of America (SSSA): &apos;http://www.soils.org/sssagloss/&apos;" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">(i) The wearing away of the land surface by rain or irrigation water, wind,ice, or other natural or anthropogenic agents that abrade, detach and removegeologic parent material or soil from one point on the earth&apos;s surface anddeposit it elsewhere, including such processes as gravitational creep andso-called tillage erosion; (ii) The detachment and movement of soil or rock bywater, wind, ice, or gravity.</skos:definition>
