    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Genomics is a field of biology focused on studying all the DNA of an organism. Such work ranges from sequencing various locations throughout a genome to identifying and characterizing all the genes and functional elements in an organism’s genome as well as how they interact.</skos:definition>
