    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="The Nature and Properties of Soils, Prentice Hall, 1996." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The soil profile is the vertical section of the soil, from the surfacethrough all its horizons, where a horizon is a layer of soil,approximately parallel to the soil surface, differing in properties andcharacteristics from adjacent layers below and above it.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2024-09-30 09:59:09.0</dcterms:modified>
