    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="http://glossary.ametsoc.org/wiki/Blowing_snow" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Snow lifted from the surface of the earth by the wind to a height of 2 m (6 ft) or more above the surface (higher than drifting snow), and blown about in such quantities that horizontal visibility is reduced to less than 11 km.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2024-10-02 09:06:15.0</dcterms:modified>
