    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Deoxyribonucleic acid (abbreviated DNA) is the double-stranded molecule that carries genetic information for the development and functioning of an organism. Whole extracted DNA from an organism or environment often referred to as gDNA (genomic).</skos:definition>
