    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Glossary of Soil Science Terms, 1996, Soil Science Society of America, Madison, WI &lt;B&gt;" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Soil Water Content: The water lost from soil upon drying to constantmass at 105 degrees Celcius; expressed either as the mass of water perunit mass of drysoil or as the volume of water per unit bulk volume ofsoil. For GCMD purpose, this also includes all measurements related tosoil water, such as capcity, potential, and pressure, etc...</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2024-09-30 10:17:49.0</dcterms:modified>
