    <skos:narrower rdf:resource="a0176a92-3eff-4278-b8db-02148c990302"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Flagellates are free-living predators and parasites bearing one toseveral flagella. The free-living types abound in freshwater or marinehabitats. Parasitic types live in the moist tissues of plants and animals,including humans.</skos:definition>
