    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-02-22 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: The transcriptome is the complete set of transcripts in a cell, and their quantity, for a specific developmental stage or physiological condition. Understanding the transcriptome is essential for interpreting the functional elements of the genome and revealing the molecular constituents of cells and tissues, and also for understanding development and disease.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
