    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">ALPHA PARTICLE FLUX</skos:prefLabel>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Porteous, A. 1996. Dictionary of Environmental Science and Technology, 2nd ed., John Wiley and Sons, NY." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An alpha particle has positive charge and consists of two protons and
two neutrons (the nucleus of a helium atom).  Alpha particles can cause 
ionization of neutral atoms.   Flux is the rate of flow through a reference
surface, measured in particles per unit area.</skos:definition>
