    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">(Also called &apos;coldness sun.&apos;) As used by the U. S. Army Corps of Engineers, the number of Fahrenheit degree-days (above and below 32°F) between the highest and lowest points on the cumulative degree-days time curve for one freezing season.</skos:definition>
