text: A principal cloud type, forming in the low levels of the troposphere and normally existing as a flat layer that does not exhibit individual elements. In aviation forecasts and reports it is coded as ST.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Bureau of Meteorology: REFERENCE MATERIAL: Glossary of Weather Terms" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A principal cloud type, forming in the low levels of the troposphere and normally existing as a flat layer that does not exhibit individual elements. In aviation forecasts and reports it is coded as ST.</skos:definition>
