Old Value=The temperature measured at a given soil depth, typically at 2, 4, 8, and
sometimes 20 and 40 in. 
Many biological processes, including seed germination, plant emergence,
microbial activity, and soil respiration are a function of soil temperature.
New Value=The temperature measured at a given soil depth, typically at 2, 4, 8, and sometimes 20 and 40 in.  Many biological processes, including seed germination, plant emergence, microbial activity, and soil respiration are a function of soil temperature.</skos:changeNote>
