    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">DROPLET DIGITAL POLYMERASE CHAIN REACTION (ddPCR)</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-02-28 User Id=tstevens Entity=PrefLabel Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
System Note=update PrefLabel
Old Value=DROPLET DIGITAL POLYMERASE CHAIN REACTION _ddPCR_
New Value=DROPLET DIGITAL POLYMERASE CHAIN REACTION (ddPCR)</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-02-28 User Id=tstevens Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=DROPLET DIGITAL POLYMERASE CHAIN REACTION _ddPCR_ [20a8731e-4a5f-4f0a-ad96-3e28274cc90a,1603386] - OMICS METHODOLOGY [d2f152e1-7398-44ad-b0a4-77ee6ef5bd6c,1603367]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-02-28 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Droplet Digital PCR (ddPCR) is a method for performing digital PCR that is based on water-oil emulsion droplet technology. A sample is fractionated into 20,000 droplets, and PCR amplification of the template molecules occurs in each individual droplet. ddPCR is a version of PCR that enables the exact quantification of nucleic acid targets within a sample.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="https://www.bio-rad.com/en-us/life-science/learning-center/introduction-to-digital-pcr/what-is-droplet-digital-pcr" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Droplet Digital PCR (ddPCR) is a method for performing digital PCR that is based on water-oil emulsion droplet technology. A sample is fractionated into 20,000 droplets, and PCR amplification of the template molecules occurs in each individual droplet. ddPCR is a version of PCR that enables the exact quantification of nucleic acid targets within a sample.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2024-02-28 15:09:48.0</dcterms:modified>
