    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Paleoclimatic information can be inferred from biogenic material in oceansediments, oxygen isotopic analyses of sea water (via deep sea cores), coralgrowth, inorganic material such as from weathering and erosion, lake levels andglacial varves, and ocean circulation changes as a result ofglacial-interglacial cycles.</skos:definition>
