    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">SUPERSATURATION</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2017-04-21 User Id=sritz Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: In meteorology, the condition existing in a given portion of the atmosphere (or other space) when the relative humidity is greater than 100%, that is, when it contains more water vapor than is needed to produce saturation with respect to a plane surface of pure water or pure ice.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2017-04-20 User Id=sritz Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=SUPERSATURATION [293cdec2-44b7-488c-ae04-0722f0a9e8b9,278819] - WATER VAPOR PROCESSES [3c4fe00c-6fb1-403e-a053-3a0174a6dfe6,278813]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Glossary of Meteorology, American Meteorological Society" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">In meteorology, the condition existing in a given portion of the atmosphere (or other space) when the relative humidity is greater than 100%, that is, when it contains more water vapor than is needed to produce saturation with respect to a plane surface of pure water or pure ice.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2017-04-21 13:02:37.0</dcterms:modified>
