    <skos:broader rdf:resource="d2f152e1-7398-44ad-b0a4-77ee6ef5bd6c"/>
    <dcterms:created>2024-02-28</dcterms:created>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">AMPLICON SEQUENCING</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-02-28 User Id=tstevens Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=AMPLICON SEQUENCING [2af266cf-69f1-4326-b54f-d161bfb4c911,1603372] - OMICS METHODOLOGY [d2f152e1-7398-44ad-b0a4-77ee6ef5bd6c,1603367]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-02-28 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Amplicon sequencing is a highly targeted approach that enables researchers to analyze genetic variation in specific genomic regions. The ultra-deep sequencing of PCR products (amplicons) allows efficient variant identification and characterization. This method uses oligonucleotide probes designed to target and capture regions of interest, followed by next-generation sequencing (NGS).
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="https://www.illumina.com/techniques/sequencing/dna-sequencing/targeted-resequencing/amplicon-sequencing.html#:~:text=Amplicon%20sequencing%20is%20a%20highly,efficient%20variant%20identification%20and%20characterization" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Amplicon sequencing is a highly targeted approach that enables researchers to analyze genetic variation in specific genomic regions. The ultra-deep sequencing of PCR products (amplicons) allows efficient variant identification and characterization. This method uses oligonucleotide probes designed to target and capture regions of interest, followed by next-generation sequencing (NGS).</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2024-02-28 11:37:18.0</dcterms:modified>
