    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The measurement of the heat flux or heat loss from open ocean areas withinthe sea ice pack is important for the study of energy balance in the polarregions and local and regional climatology. Heat loss through the openwater is 100 times more than through thick ice.</skos:definition>
