    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">GOES WIND INDEX</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2017-04-21 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: A GOES sounder-derived parameter used for estimating the maximum convective wind gusts is the Wind Index (WINDEX). The Wind Index is plotted on regional GOES images (visible, infrared, or water vapor) and made available on the GOES Microburst Products web page.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2017-04-20 User Id=sritz Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=GOES WIND INDEX [8251fedc-3910-4f18-9594-df2fbb9bb1d9,278905] - WIND INDICES [25775905-dac3-4834-b709-f38a0a03b258,278861]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Pryor K., Ellrod G., Bailey A., Recent Improvements to the GOES Wind Index, NOAA NESDIS, 2002. Recent Improvements to the GOES Wind Index" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A GOES sounder-derived parameter used for estimating the maximum convective wind gusts is the Wind Index (WINDEX). The Wind Index is plotted on regional GOES images (visible, infrared, or water vapor) and made available on the GOES Microburst Products web page.</skos:definition>
