    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-03-11 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: The change of air temperature with height above the ground. When the temperature increases with height, the profile is called an inversion profile, or simply an inversion. When the temperature decreases strongly with height, a convective profile may be established.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="San Diego State University" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The change of air temperature with height above the ground. When the temperature increases with height, the profile is called an inversion profile, or simply an inversion. When the temperature decreases strongly with height, a convective profile may be established.</skos:definition>
