    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">BIN/BINNING</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-02-28 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: A bin is a subset of genomic fragments that are believed to be from the same species in a metagenomic community. Contig binning aims to put the assembled genomic fragments, or contigs, from the same genome into the same bin. The contigs from these bins are then presented as a single collection to form metagenome-assembled genomes (MAGs).
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-02-28 User Id=tstevens Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=BIN/BINNING [3078eaeb-541e-44a0-9828-a1020f7bc6cf,1603374] - OMICS METHODOLOGY [d2f152e1-7398-44ad-b0a4-77ee6ef5bd6c,1603367]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="https://genomebiology.biomedcentral.com/articles/10.1186/s13059-022-02832-6" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A bin is a subset of genomic fragments that are believed to be from the same species in a metagenomic community. Contig binning aims to put the assembled genomic fragments, or contigs, from the same genome into the same bin. The contigs from these bins are then presented as a single collection to form metagenome-assembled genomes (MAGs).</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2024-02-28 11:39:48.0</dcterms:modified>
