    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">ADVECTION FOG</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-03-21 User Id=mpmorahan Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: A type of fog caused by the advection of moist air over a cold surface, and the consequent cooling of that air to below its dewpoint.

A very common advection fog is that caused by moist air over a cold body of water (sea fog).

Sometimes applied to steam fog.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
