    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A type of fog caused by the advection of moist air over a cold surface, and the consequent cooling of that air to below its dewpoint.A very common advection fog is that caused by moist air over a cold body of water (sea fog).Sometimes applied to steam fog.</skos:definition>
