text: A fall wind with a source so cold that, when the air reaches the lowlands or coast, the dynamic warming is insufficient to raise the air temperature to the normal level for the region; hence it appears as a cold wind.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Glossary of Meteorology, American Meteorological Society" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A fall wind with a source so cold that, when the air reaches the lowlands or coast, the dynamic warming is insufficient to raise the air temperature to the normal level for the region; hence it appears as a cold wind.</skos:definition>
