    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">BIRTH RATE DECLINE/INCREASE</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-10-08 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=reference 
System Note=update Definition
New Value=https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/references/definitions-and-notes/</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-10-08 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Refers to the decline and increase of the birth rate. Birth rate, also known as natality, is the total number of live human births per 1,000 population for a given period divided by the length of the period in years.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-06-26 User Id=gee-cee Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=BIRTH RATE DECLINE/INCREASE [379dd4c3-04d7-4f76-9bb9-83d0b8e1a2aa,39885] - BIOSPHERIC INDICATORS [76943142-e5a9-4ecf-b496-050dd3d97101,39883]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/references/definitions-and-notes/" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Refers to the decline and increase of the birth rate. Birth rate, also known as natality, is the total number of live human births per 1,000 population for a given period divided by the length of the period in years.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2024-10-08 13:53:13.0</dcterms:modified>
