    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Finite Time Lyapunov Exponent</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2025-05-22 User Id=tstevens Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=Finite Time Lyapunov Exponent [34033240-5675-4760-9fad-0c0d9b67b7ce,2164038] - OCEAN CIRCULATION [a031952d-9f00-4ba5-9966-5f87ab9dfdd4,2160676]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2025-05-22 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
System Note=update Definition
New Value=The Finite-Time Lyapunov Exponent (FTLE) is a well-established numerical tool for assessing stretching rates of initial parcels of fluid. FTLE is referenced as part of the Global multi-scale Eulerian and Lagrangian oceanic 2 environmental variables for the period 2000-2009.</skos:changeNote>
