Works. 1998. Prentice-Hall, Inc. Upper Saddle River, New Jersey.
New Value=Nebel, Bernard J.and Richard T. Wright. Environmental Science-the Way the World Works. 1998. Prentice-Hall, Inc. Upper Saddle River, New Jersey.</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2017-03-15 User Id=mgenazzi Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
User Note=Definition updated
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=Chlorophyll is the green pigment in plants responsible for absorbing the
light energy required for photosynthesis.
New Value=Chlorophyll is the green pigment in plants responsible for absorbing the light energy required for photosynthesis.</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Nebel, Bernard J.and Richard T. Wright. Environmental Science-the Way the World Works. 1998. Prentice-Hall, Inc. Upper Saddle River, New Jersey." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Chlorophyll is the green pigment in plants responsible for absorbing the light energy required for photosynthesis.</skos:definition>
