    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">SEALS/SEA LIONS/WALRUSES</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2017-03-15 User Id=mgenazzi Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Definition added
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Phylum Chordata. Class Mammalia. Order Carnivora. Pinnipeds are widely distributed carnivorous, fin-footed, marine mammals. Seals are eared and use well developed fore-flippers for swimming and walking. Sea lions have external ear flaps. Walruses are characterized by their tusks and whiskers.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="marinemammalcenter.org" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Phylum Chordata. Class Mammalia. Order Carnivora. Pinnipeds are widely distributed carnivorous, fin-footed, marine mammals. Seals are eared and use well developed fore-flippers for swimming and walking. Sea lions have external ear flaps. Walruses are characterized by their tusks and whiskers.</skos:definition>
