    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Adapted from Allaby, Michael. 1998. A Dictionary of Plant Sciences, New York: Oxford University Press." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">&apos;Macrobiota&apos; is a general term for the larger soil organisms. Macrofauna, inparticular, refers to burrowing vertebrate animals, but may include largerinsects and earhworms.</skos:definition>
