    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Talik, also called tabetisol, is a Russian term applied to permanently unfrozenground in regions of permafrost. &lt;p&gt;This usually applies to a layer that lies above the permafrost but below theactive layer, that is, when the permafrost table is deeper than the depthreached by winter freezing from the surface. Talik is also found within andbeneath permafrost; when it occurs beneath the permafrost it is equivalent tosubgelisol.</skos:definition>
