    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-03-21 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=A naturally occurring, usually inorganic substance that is not considered to be
amineral because it is amorphous and lacks a periodically repeating arrangement
of atoms, e.g. opal.  
Syn: gel mineral
New Value=A naturally occurring, usually inorganic substance that is not considered to be a mineral because it is amorphous and lacks a periodically repeating arrangement of atoms, e.g. opal.</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-03-21 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=reference 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=Jackson, J.A. (1997) &lt;i&gt;Glossary of Geology&lt;/i&gt;. 4th ed. Alexandria,
VA: American Geological Institute. 769 p.
New Value=American Geological Institute</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="American Geological Institute" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A naturally occurring, usually inorganic substance that is not considered to be a mineral because it is amorphous and lacks a periodically repeating arrangement of atoms, e.g. opal.</skos:definition>
