    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Adapted from the ​EM-DAT International Disaster Database (https://www.emdat.be/classification)" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Mapping of ​hazards caused by exposure to living organisms and their toxic substances (e.g., venom, mold) or vector-borne diseases that they may carry. Examples are venomous wildlife and insects, poisonous plants, and mosquitoes carrying disease-causing agents such as parasites, bacteria, or viruses (e.g., malaria).</skos:definition>
