    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A chemical element that is a shiny gray solid and has the same electron configuration in the outer electron shell and a similar crystal structure. Magnesium is the ninth most abundant element in the universe. It is produced in large, aging stars from the sequential addition of three helium nuclei to a carbon nucleus.</skos:definition>
