    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Adapted from the IPCC TAR (https://www.ipcc.ch/site/assets/uploads/2018/03/TAR-07.pdf) and the USGCRP Glossary (https://www.globalchange.gov/climate-change/glossary)" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Processes within the cryosphere through which the climate system iscontrolled, changed, or modulated. Cryospheric feedbacks involve aperturbation in a climate quantity that causes a change in a secondquantity, and the change in the second quantity ultimately leads to anadditional change in the first. Cryospheric feedbacks may, for example,involve the dependence of surface albedo on the presence of ice andsnow.</skos:definition>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
