    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">TOWERING CUMULUS</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-03-21 User Id=mpmorahan Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: A vertically developed cumulus cloud, often a precursor to cumulonimbus. In aviation forecasts and reports it is coded as TCU.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-02-14 User Id=mpmorahan Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=TOWERING CUMULUS [79668331-c50d-49da-aea6-83c94545f9e3,82225] - CUMULUS CONGESTUS [3bafe2e0-c1a7-4bee-a02e-ac66964b4d7f,82223]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Bureau of Meteorology: REFERENCE MATERIAL: Glossary of Weather Terms" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A vertically developed cumulus cloud, often a precursor to cumulonimbus. In aviation forecasts and reports it is coded as TCU.</skos:definition>
