    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">OIL SPILLS</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-07-11 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=reference 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=Chiras, Daniel D. 1998. Environmental Science.	A Systems Approach to
Sustainable Development. Wadsworth Publishing Company. Belmont, California.
New Value=Chiras, Daniel D. 1998. Environmental Science. A Systems Approach to Sustainable Development. Wadsworth Publishing Company. Belmont, California.</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-07-11 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=A Oil Spill is defined not only as oil which comes from wrecked
tankers that spill out oil, but also to oil which comes from well
blowouts, breaks in pipelines or oil that enters the oceans from the
transfer of oil from offshore platforms to shore during normal operations.
New Value=An oil spill is defined not only as oil which comes from wrecked tankers that spill out oil, but also to oil which comes from well blowouts, breaks in pipelines or oil that enters the oceans from the transfer of oil from offshore platforms to shore during normal operations.</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-06-27 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=PrefLabel Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
System Note=update PrefLabel
Old Value=OIL SPILL
New Value=OIL SPILLS</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Chiras, Daniel D. 1998. Environmental Science. A Systems Approach to Sustainable Development. Wadsworth Publishing Company. Belmont, California." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An oil spill is defined not only as oil which comes from wrecked tankers that spill out oil, but also to oil which comes from well blowouts, breaks in pipelines or oil that enters the oceans from the transfer of oil from offshore platforms to shore during normal operations.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2012-07-11 10:03:46.0</dcterms:modified>
