New Value=Karr, J. R. (1981), Assessment of Biotic Integrity Using Fish Communities. Fisheries, 6: 21–27. doi:10.1577/1548-8446(1981)006&lt;0021:AOBIUF&gt;2.0.CO;2</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2018-03-07 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=A measure of water quality based on the presence of Benthic organisms.
New Value=A scientific tool used to identify and classify water pollution problems. An Index of Biotic Integrity (IBI) associates anthropogenic influences on a water body with biological activity in the water body, and is formulated using data developed from biosurveys.</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2018-03-07 User Id=tstevens Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Move Concepts
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=BENTHIC INDEX [4497eb1b-b64d-46ff-a18d-37d217430777,86785] - WATER QUALITY INDEXES [f2130ca3-3587-4312-b6d4-138456b5ea78,310635]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Karr, J. R. (1981), Assessment of Biotic Integrity Using Fish Communities. Fisheries, 6: 21–27. doi:10.1577/1548-8446(1981)006&lt;0021:AOBIUF&gt;2.0.CO;2" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A scientific tool used to identify and classify water pollution problems. An Index of Biotic Integrity (IBI) associates anthropogenic influences on a water body with biological activity in the water body, and is formulated using data developed from biosurveys.</skos:definition>
