    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">LEAD</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2018-03-07 User Id=tstevens Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=LEAD [6fe420c1-2285-4031-babe-f0243c59a617,310669] - CONTAMINANTS [42c6d91b-afef-4638-95c5-0d130828b2e7,84623]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2018-03-07 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: A chemical element and a heavy metal that is denser than most common materials. Lead is soft and malleable, and has a relatively low melting point. When freshly cut, lead is bluish-white; it tarnishes to a dull gray color when exposed to air. Lead has the highest atomic number of any stable element and concludes three major decay chains of heavier elements.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Oxford University Press" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A chemical element and a heavy metal that is denser than most common materials. Lead is soft and malleable, and has a relatively low melting point. When freshly cut, lead is bluish-white; it tarnishes to a dull gray color when exposed to air. Lead has the highest atomic number of any stable element and concludes three major decay chains of heavier elements.</skos:definition>
