    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">ANCHOVIES/HERRINGS</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2017-03-15 User Id=mgenazzi Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Definition added
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Phylum Chordata. Class Actinopterygii. Order Clupeiformes. Anchovies, Family Engraulidae, are small common salt-water forage fish with a large mouth, characterized by a blunt snout with teeth in both jaws and a rostral organ. Herring, Family Clupediae, are small common salt-water forage fish characterized by a single dorsal fin without spines, no lateral line and protruding lower jaw.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="encyclopedia of life" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Phylum Chordata. Class Actinopterygii. Order Clupeiformes. Anchovies, Family Engraulidae, are small common salt-water forage fish with a large mouth, characterized by a blunt snout with teeth in both jaws and a rostral organ. Herring, Family Clupediae, are small common salt-water forage fish characterized by a single dorsal fin without spines, no lateral line and protruding lower jaw.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2017-03-15 08:43:05.0</dcterms:modified>
