    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">BIOINFORMATICS</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-02-28 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Bioinformatics, as related to genetics and genomics, is a scientific subdiscipline that involves using computer technology to collect, store, analyze, and disseminate biological data and information, such as DNA and amino acid sequences or annotations about those sequences. Scientists and clinicians use databases that organize and index such biological information to increase our understanding of health and disease and, in certain cases, as part of medical care.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-02-28 User Id=tstevens Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=BIOINFORMATICS [41f960a3-d695-4fa2-bfad-2d2887e1b063,1603381] - OMICS METHODOLOGY [d2f152e1-7398-44ad-b0a4-77ee6ef5bd6c,1603367]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="https://www.genome.gov/genetics-glossary/Bioinformatics" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Bioinformatics, as related to genetics and genomics, is a scientific subdiscipline that involves using computer technology to collect, store, analyze, and disseminate biological data and information, such as DNA and amino acid sequences or annotations about those sequences. Scientists and clinicians use databases that organize and index such biological information to increase our understanding of health and disease and, in certain cases, as part of medical care.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2024-02-28 14:50:54.0</dcterms:modified>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="426aee98-764c-4c21-ab65-1e9d4bd6b0d0">
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="77397026-09c9-44e0-b85f-77b2bc9b1630"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">TROPOSPHERIC OZONE</skos:prefLabel>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Glossary of Meteorology, American Meteorological Society, 1998." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Ozone (O3) that is measured  in the lowest 10-20 km of the Atmosphere.While the maximum concentration of ozone occurs between 20-25 km, ahigh concentration of ozone close to the Earth&apos;s surface is considered apublic health threat.</skos:definition>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
  </skos:Concept>
