    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-10-24 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=Pertaining to the measurement of isotopic (excluding oxygen) signatures
in ocean/lake sediments to determine past climatic conditions, and apply
those findings to the Earth&apos;s climate at the time period in question.
Carbon isotope analysis is very important in extracting paleoclimatic
signatures from corals and from benthic forams.
New Value=Pertaining to the measurement of isotopic (excluding oxygen) signatures
in ocean/lake sediments to determine past climatic conditions, and apply
those findings to the Earth&apos;s climate at the time period in question.
Carbon isotope analysis is very important in extracting paleoclimatic
signatures from corals and from benthic forams.</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Bradley, R.S. 1999. Paleoclimatology: Reconstructing Climates of the Quaternary, 2nd edition. Harcourt Academic Press." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Pertaining to the measurement of isotopic (excluding oxygen) signaturesin ocean/lake sediments to determine past climatic conditions, and applythose findings to the Earth&apos;s climate at the time period in question.Carbon isotope analysis is very important in extracting paleoclimaticsignatures from corals and from benthic forams.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2024-10-24 09:02:07.0</dcterms:modified>
