    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Adapted from A Dictionary of Biology, Oxford, 1996, 3rd edition." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Species which transfer pollen from an anther (the male reproductive organ) 
to a stigma (the receptive part of the female reproductive organ), either 
of the same flower (self-pollinator) or of a different flower of the same 
species (cross-pollinator).</skos:definition>
