New Value=id: null
text: Environmental DNA (eDNA) is organismal DNA that can be found in the environment and originates from cellular material shed by larger organisms (via skin, excrement, etc.) into aquatic or terrestrial environments, or can represent the entirety of smaller organisms present within the sample.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="https://www.usgs.gov/special-topics/water-science-school/science/environmental-dna-edna" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Environmental DNA (eDNA) is organismal DNA that can be found in the environment and originates from cellular material shed by larger organisms (via skin, excrement, etc.) into aquatic or terrestrial environments, or can represent the entirety of smaller organisms present within the sample.</skos:definition>
