  <skos:Concept rdf:about="5e9ad407-bd70-43ae-a901-6b07f100db27">
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="4e4d3c18-cdd4-474a-a936-6e127ec526f7"/>
    <dcterms:created>2021-10-20</dcterms:created>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">SWELL HEIGHT</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2021-10-20 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: The estimated average height of the highest one-third of the swells.  It is estimated from determining how the wave energy is distributed among various periods (frequencies), determining if a separate swell energy peak exists, and then, picking a frequency to separate swell and wind-waves. The swell height is calculated from the wave energies below the separation frequency.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2021-10-20 User Id=tstevens Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=SWELL HEIGHT [5e9ad407-bd70-43ae-a901-6b07f100db27,778219] - SWELLS [4e4d3c18-cdd4-474a-a936-6e127ec526f7,776184]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="https://www.ndbc.noaa.gov/waveobs.shtml" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The estimated average height of the highest one-third of the swells.  It is estimated from determining how the wave energy is distributed among various periods (frequencies), determining if a separate swell energy peak exists, and then, picking a frequency to separate swell and wind-waves. The swell height is calculated from the wave energies below the separation frequency.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2021-10-20 15:06:05.0</dcterms:modified>
