    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">SPITS AND BARS</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-03-29 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: A deposition landform  found off coasts. At one end, spits connect to land, while at the far end they exist in open water. A spit is a type of bar or beach that develops where a re-entrant occurs, such as at cove&apos;s headlands, by the process of longshore drift.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-02-18 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
