System Note=update Definition
Old Value=Any radioactive form of a chemical element, having the same atomic weight
as that element (i.e. same number of protons), but a different number of
neutrons. Used in a variety of oceanic applications such as dating and
movement of water masses.
New Value=Any radioactive form of a chemical element, having the same atomic weight as that element (i.e. same number of protons), but a different number of neutrons. Used in a variety of oceanic applications such as dating and
movement of water masses.</skos:changeNote>
