System Note=delete broader relation
Old Value=CLOUD HEIGHT [57292a97-19be-4fae-b2f7-9fa0a3629b53,63281] - CLOUDS [162e2243-3266-4999-b352-d8a1a9dc82ac,62017]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Glickman,T.S., ed. 2000.Glossary of Weather and Climate, 2nd ed., American Meteorological Society, Boston, MA" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">In weather observations, the height of the cloud base above localterrain.  In satellite remote sensing, cloud height is often referred to as theheight of the cloud top above local terrain or above mean sea level. Also canbe defined as the vertical distance from the cloud base to the cloud top; morecommonly referred to as the &apos;thickness&apos; or &apos;depth&apos; of the cloud. </skos:definition>
