    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Glossary of Meteorology, American Meteorological Society, 2017." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The anvil-shaped cloud that comprises the upper portion of mature cumulonimbus clouds; the popular name given to a cumulonimbus capillatus cloud, particularly if it embodies the supplementary feature incus (from the Latin for anvil).</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2017-03-16 10:17:36.0</dcterms:modified>
