    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Harvard University" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The separation of minerals into different components. Mineral dissolution and precipitation, especially of Fe and Mn (hydr)oxides and the carbonate mineral family, partially regulate pH and alkalinity of natural waters, affecting the fate and transport of organic and inorganic contaminants.</skos:definition>
