    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-03-11 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=The geiod is the equipotential surface of the Earth&apos;s gravity field which best
fits, in a least squares sense, global mean sea level.	 Geoid properties
refers to parameters, such as height, used to describe the geoid.
New Value=Describes the gravitational properties of the geoid, which is defined as a surface on which the earth&apos;s attractive (i.e. gravitational) forces are everywhere equal, i.e. a gravimetric equipotential surface. The geoid is of fundamental importance in determining positions on the earth&apos;s surface as most measurements are made with reference to this surface.</skos:changeNote>
