    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Describes the gravitational properties of the geoid, which is defined as a surface on which the earth&apos;s attractive (i.e. gravitational) forces are everywhere equal, i.e. a gravimetric equipotential surface. The geoid is of fundamental importance in determining positions on the earth&apos;s surface as most measurements are made with reference to this surface.</skos:definition>
