    <skos:narrower rdf:resource="940550d2-1d9f-4c28-b9ba-857c2dc8ef95"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">To measure sea surface height, or surface topography, scientists needto obtain the precise distance between the satellite and the center ofthe Earth and the precise distance between the satellite and the seasurface. Sea surface height is then calculated by subtracting thedistance between the sea surface and the satellite from the distancebetween the center of the Earth and the satellite. The distance betweenthe satellite and the center of the Earth is obtained by carefullymonitoring the satellite position at all times.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2021-10-22 12:44:26.0</dcterms:modified>
