    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-04-01 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: The formation process of firn, a partially compacted névé, which is a type of snow that has been left over from past seasons and has been recrystallized into a substance denser than névé. It is ice that is at an intermediate stage between snow and glacial ice.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="USGS" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The formation process of firn, a partially compacted névé, which is a type of snow that has been left over from past seasons and has been recrystallized into a substance denser than névé. It is ice that is at an intermediate stage between snow and glacial ice.</skos:definition>
