    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">WEATHERING</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-04-01 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Breaking down of Earth&apos;s rocks, soils and minerals through direct contact with the planet&apos;s atmosphere. Weathering occurs in situ, or &quot;with no movement&quot;, and thus should not be confused with erosion, which involves the movement of rocks and minerals by agents such as water, ice, wind, and gravity.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-03-05 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=WEATHERING [580ef100-0fb8-456c-a9ca-565d11392a26,82819] - GLACIAL PROCESSES [d7b62912-5970-46b1-be45-6a603c9a6979,82723]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="PhysicalGeography.net" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Breaking down of Earth&apos;s rocks, soils and minerals through direct contact with the planet&apos;s atmosphere. Weathering occurs in situ, or &apos;with no movement&apos;, and thus should not be confused with erosion, which involves the movement of rocks and minerals by agents such as water, ice, wind, and gravity.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2013-04-01 11:28:00.0</dcterms:modified>
