    <skos:changeNote>Date=2021-09-02 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=Carbon is one of three important elements that compose plants.	The
higher photosynthetic organisms need light, carbon dioxide, and water and
these raw materials supply the carbon, oxygen, and hydrogen that are the
predominant elements in the organic molecules they manufacture, as well as
the energy needed to drive the synthetic reactions.
New Value=Any measurement of Carbon in the soil, in organic or inorganic fractions.</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2021-09-02 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=reference 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=Gould, J. and W.Keaton. 1996. Biological Science. W.W. Norton and Company. New
York, New York.
New Value=United States Department of Agriculture</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="United States Department of Agriculture" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Any measurement of Carbon in the soil, in organic or inorganic fractions.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2024-09-26 10:04:20.0</dcterms:modified>
