    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="American Chemical Society" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The process by which a solid or liquid forms a solution in a solvent. In solids this can be explained as the breakdown of the crystal lattice into individual ions, atoms or molecules and their transport into the solvent.</skos:definition>
