    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">GLACIAL DISPLACEMENT</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-10-30 User Id=tstevens Entity=WeightedRelation Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert WeightedRelation
New Value=id: null
related concept uuid: 5ddbaf71-b279-42cf-b250-faaefb627f66
relationship type: null
relationship value: null
generated by: null</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-04-01 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: The displacement of a glacier. The speed of glacial displacement is partly determined by friction. Friction makes the ice at the bottom of the glacier move slower than the upper portion. In alpine glaciers, friction is also generated at the valley&apos;s side walls, which slows the edges relative to the center.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-03-05 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=GLACIAL DISPLACEMENT [5ddbaf71-b279-42cf-b250-faaefb627f66,82799] - GLACIAL PROCESSES [d7b62912-5970-46b1-be45-6a603c9a6979,82723]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="PhysicalGeography.net" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The displacement of a glacier. The speed of glacial displacement is partly determined by friction. Friction makes the ice at the bottom of the glacier move slower than the upper portion. In alpine glaciers, friction is also generated at the valley&apos;s side walls, which slows the edges relative to the center.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2024-10-30 08:05:07.0</dcterms:modified>
