text: Phylum Chordata. Class Mammalia. Family Ursidae. Bears are canivoran mammals with large bodies, stocky legs, log snouts, small rounded ears, shaggy hairs distinguished by plantigrade paw with five nonretractile claws and short tails.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="encyclopedia of life" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Phylum Chordata. Class Mammalia. Family Ursidae. Bears are canivoran mammals with large bodies, stocky legs, log snouts, small rounded ears, shaggy hairs distinguished by plantigrade paw with five nonretractile claws and short tails.</skos:definition>
