    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">INDICATOR SPECIES</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-07-10 User Id=mpmorahan Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: A species whose presence, absence, or relative well-being in a given environment is a sign of the overall health of its ecosystem. By monitoring the condition and behavior of an indicator species, scientists can determine how changes in the environment are likely to affect other species that are more difficult to study.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-06-26 User Id=gee-cee Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=INDICATOR SPECIES [6448f172-1560-4ea7-8826-8ac85dc820f3,39893] - BIOSPHERIC INDICATORS [76943142-e5a9-4ecf-b496-050dd3d97101,39883]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="The American Heritage® Science Dictionary, 2010, by Houghton Mifflin Harcourt Publishing Company. Published by Houghton Mifflin Harcourt Publishing Company." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A species whose presence, absence, or relative well-being in a given environment is a sign of the overall health of its ecosystem. By monitoring the condition and behavior of an indicator species, scientists can determine how changes in the environment are likely to affect other species that are more difficult to study.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2012-07-10 09:35:22.0</dcterms:modified>
