    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/B9780128022344000021" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Sanger sequencing, also known as the chain termination method, is a technique for DNA sequencing based upon the selective incorporation of chain-terminating dideoxynucleotides (ddNTPs) by DNA polymerase during in vitro DNA replication.</skos:definition>
