    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">SWAMPS</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2017-03-15 User Id=mgenazzi Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Definition added
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: An area of land that is always soaked with water; low, wet land that supports grass and trees. Swamps are wet areas that are normally covered by water all year and subject to drying out during the summer.  The parameter Swamp may be colloquially interchanged with the parameter Marshes.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="PhysicalGeography.net" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An area of land that is always soaked with water; low, wet land that supports grass and trees. Swamps are wet areas that are normally covered by water all year and subject to drying out during the summer.  The parameter Swamp may be colloquially interchanged with the parameter Marshes.</skos:definition>
