    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Adapted from the IPCC TAR (https://www.ipcc.ch/site/assets/uploads/2018/03/TAR-07.pdf) and the USGCRP Glossary (https://www.globalchange.gov/climate-change/glossary)" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Processes or interactions between systems, such as the ocean andatmosphere, through which the climate system is controlled, changed,or modulated. Examples include process that influence the flux of heat,freshwater, and radiatively active trace gases between the ocean andatmosphere as well as those that influence the exchange of carbondioxide between the atmosphere and terrestrial biosphere.</skos:definition>
