    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">PLATE TECTONICS</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-07-26 User Id=mpmorahan Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: a theory in geology: the lithosphere of the earth is divided into a small number of plates which float on and travel independently over the mantle and much of the earth&apos;s seismic activity occurs at the boundaries of these plates
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-07-26 User Id=mpmorahan Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=a theory in geology: the lithosphere of the earth is divided into a small number of plates which float on and travel independently over the mantle and much of the earth&apos;s seismic activity occurs at the boundaries of these plates
New Value=A theory of global tectonics in which the lithosphere is divided into a number of plates whose pattern of horizontal movement is that of torsionally rigid bodies that interact with one another at their boundaries, causing seismic and tectonic activity along these boundaries.</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-07-26 User Id=mpmorahan Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=reference 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=MERRIAM-WEBSTER ONLINE - http://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/plate%20tectonics
New Value=Jackson, J.A.(1997) Glossary of Geology. 4th ed. Alexandria, VA:American Geological Institute.769 p.</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-06-26 User Id=gee-cee Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=PLATE TECTONICS [6971fecc-af14-4c97-82db-2b01c98453b9,40087] - PALEOCLIMATE INDICATORS [c9a5b3eb-7556-41a8-a2b8-c015db80e5b2,39947]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Jackson, J.A.(1997) Glossary of Geology. 4th ed. Alexandria, VA:American Geological Institute.769 p." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A theory of global tectonics in which the lithosphere is divided into a number of plates whose pattern of horizontal movement is that of torsionally rigid bodies that interact with one another at their boundaries, causing seismic and tectonic activity along these boundaries.</skos:definition>
