    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="PhysicalGeography.net" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An area of highland, usually consisting of relatively flat terrain. A highly eroded plateau is called a dissected plateau. A volcanic plateau is a plateau produced by volcanic activity.</skos:definition>
