    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">WATER HARDNESS</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2018-03-07 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: A condition caused predominantly by dissolved salts of calcium, magnesium and iron, such as bicarbonates, carbonates, sulfates, chlorides and nitrates, a water-quality indicator of the concentration of alkaline salts in water, hard water requires more soap, detergent or shampoo to raise a lather.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2018-03-07 User Id=tstevens Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=WATER HARDNESS [75a83951-a086-4d25-9ab0-c118b0e20383,310689] - WATER CHARACTERISTICS [f7e97dc3-1181-41b5-8b90-946eb2504110,310633]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="British Columbia Environmental Protection Division Glossary of Water Quality Terms" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A condition caused predominantly by dissolved salts of calcium, magnesium and iron, such as bicarbonates, carbonates, sulfates, chlorides and nitrates, a water-quality indicator of the concentration of alkaline salts in water, hard water requires more soap, detergent or shampoo to raise a lather.</skos:definition>
