  <skos:Concept rdf:about="772d8044-f11b-4b01-bc72-d7dd45cfe1b3">
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="7c4d5f8f-4809-4859-b379-3b8c379bc83c"/>
    <dcterms:created>2013-02-14</dcterms:created>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">PYROCUMULONIMBUS</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-03-20 User Id=mpmorahan Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Pyrocumulonimbus is the fire-breathing dragon of clouds. A cumulonimbus without the &quot;&quot;pyre&quot;&quot; part is imposing enough -- a massive, anvil-shaped tower of power reaching five miles (8 km) high, hurling thunderbolts, wind and rain.

Add smoke and fire to the mix and you have pyrocumulonimbus, an explosive storm cloud actually created by the smoke and heat from fire, and which can ravage tens of thousands of acres. And in the process, &quot;&quot;pyroCb&quot;&quot; storms funnel their smoke like a chimney into Earth&apos;s stratosphere, with lingering ill effects.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-02-14 User Id=mpmorahan Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=PYROCUMULONIMBUS [772d8044-f11b-4b01-bc72-d7dd45cfe1b3,82213] - CUMULONIMBUS [7c4d5f8f-4809-4859-b379-3b8c379bc83c,82205]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="NASA http://www.nasa.gov/topics/earth/features/pyrocb.html&apos;" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Pyrocumulonimbus is the fire-breathing dragon of clouds. A cumulonimbus without the &apos;&apos;pyre&apos;&apos; part is imposing enough -- a massive, anvil-shaped tower of power reaching five miles (8 km) high, hurling thunderbolts, wind and rain.Add smoke and fire to the mix and you have pyrocumulonimbus, an explosive storm cloud actually created by the smoke and heat from fire, and which can ravage tens of thousands of acres. And in the process, &apos;&apos;pyroCb&apos;&apos; storms funnel their smoke like a chimney into Earth&apos;s stratosphere, with lingering ill effects.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2013-03-20 19:01:07.0</dcterms:modified>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
  </skos:Concept>
