  <skos:Concept rdf:about="77b2422e-ce52-465f-8841-5d04ebe536dc">
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="b887d3e5-4280-43d2-a34e-0f63ac086b6a"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">NORTHERN OSCILLATION INDEX</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-07-09 User Id=mpmorahan Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: The NOI (extratropical-based Northern Oscillation Index) and its analog, the SOI* (extratropical-bassed Southern Oscillation Index) are new indices of midlatitude climate fluctuations that show interesting relationships with fluctuations in marine ecosystems and populations. They reflect the variability in equatorial and extratropical teleconnections and represent a wide range of local and remote climate signals. The indices are counterparts to the traditional SOI (Southern Oscillation Index) that relate variability in the atmospheric forcing of climate change in northern and southern midlatitude hemisphere regions.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-06-25 User Id=mpmorahan Entity=NarrowerRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add narrower relation
New Value=NORTHERN OSCILLATION INDEX [77b2422e-ce52-465f-8841-5d04ebe536dc,22999] - NOI [9a43235b-a7b7-4c76-b296-c01799b1f278,39697]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2020-02-14 User Id=tstevens Entity=NarrowerRelation Operation=DELETE 
User Note=Remove Concepts
System Note=delete narrower relation
Old Value=NORTHERN OSCILLATION INDEX [77b2422e-ce52-465f-8841-5d04ebe536dc,86449] - NOI [9a43235b-a7b7-4c76-b296-c01799b1f278,86855]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Text Source: NOAA Environmental Research Division, http://www.pfeg.noaa.gov/products/PFEL/modeled/indices/NOIx/noix.html" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The NOI (extratropical-based Northern Oscillation Index) and its analog, the SOI* (extratropical-bassed Southern Oscillation Index) are new indices of midlatitude climate fluctuations that show interesting relationships with fluctuations in marine ecosystems and populations. They reflect the variability in equatorial and extratropical teleconnections and represent a wide range of local and remote climate signals. The indices are counterparts to the traditional SOI (Southern Oscillation Index) that relate variability in the atmospheric forcing of climate change in northern and southern midlatitude hemisphere regions.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2020-02-14 15:22:42.0</dcterms:modified>
