    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">CORAL REEF EXTENT</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2021-10-19 User Id=tstevens Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=CORAL REEF EXTENT [7e24064a-7035-402a-ab9d-fa5e5c359720,778191] - CORAL REEFS [ad497e7a-48fa-45e1-90a5-b052508bdb30,775014]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2021-10-19 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Measurement of the spatial extent or dimensions of coral reefs. A coral reef is an underwater ecosystem characterized by reef-building corals. Reefs are formed by colonies of coral polyps held together by calcium carbonate. They are most commonly found at shallow depths in tropical waters, but deep water and cold water coral reefs exist on smaller scales in other areas.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Goodman, James A., Samuel J. Purkis, and Stuart R. Phinn, (Eds). Coral Reef Remote Sensing. 2013. Springer. DOI 10.1007/978-90-481-9292-2" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Measurement of the spatial extent or dimensions of coral reefs. A coral reef is an underwater ecosystem characterized by reef-building corals. Reefs are formed by colonies of coral polyps held together by calcium carbonate. They are most commonly found at shallow depths in tropical waters, but deep water and cold water coral reefs exist on smaller scales in other areas.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2021-10-19 08:42:45.0</dcterms:modified>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
  </skos:Concept>
