    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Alyn C. Duxbury, Alison B. Duxbury, and Keith A. Sverdrup. An Introduction to the World&apos;s Oceans. 6th edition. McGraw-Hill Higher Education, 2000." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Isolated steep-sided volcanic peak that rises abruptly at least 1000 m from thesea floor, sometimes piercing the surface to become islands.</skos:definition>
