    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Glickman, T.S., ed. 2000 Glossary of Meteorology, 2nd ed., American Meteorological Society, Boston, MA" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The height ascribed to the lowest layer of clouds or obscurring phenomenawhen it is reported as broken (5/8 to 7/8 coverage), overcast, or obscurationand not classified &apos;thin&apos; or &apos;partial&apos;.  Expressed in above ground level (AGL)heights. See also the definitions for cloud height and cloud base.</skos:definition>
